WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.606
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.906 --> 00:00:09.408
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.708 --> 00:00:16.447
Unit eight: Present Perfect Continuous. Today you will talk about actions that started in the past and continue now.

4
00:00:16.747 --> 00:00:19.202
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:23.434
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.283 --> 00:00:25.238
Have been.

7
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:30.479
Have been means the helper for I, you, we and they in the perfect continuous.

8
00:00:31.083 --> 00:00:32.433
I have been studying.

9
00:00:33.017 --> 00:00:35.866
Your turn. Say: Have been.

10
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:39.922
Have been.

11
00:00:40.683 --> 00:00:41.742
Has been.

12
00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:47.130
Has been means the helper for he, she and it in the perfect continuous.

13
00:00:47.717 --> 00:00:49.031
She has been working.

14
00:00:49.617 --> 00:00:51.956
Your turn. Say: Has been.

15
00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:55.778
Has been.

16
00:00:56.517 --> 00:00:57.262
-ing.

17
00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:01.469
-ing means the ending that shows an action in progress.

18
00:01:02.083 --> 00:01:03.317
Working, studying.

19
00:01:03.917 --> 00:01:06.581
Your turn. Say: -ing.

20
00:01:09.433 --> 00:01:10.144
-ing.

21
00:01:10.883 --> 00:01:11.896
Duration.

22
00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:15.359
Duration means how long something lasts.

23
00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:17.694
The duration is two hours.

24
00:01:18.283 --> 00:01:20.599
Your turn. Say: Duration.

25
00:01:23.433 --> 00:01:24.400
Duration.

26
00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:26.105
Since.

27
00:01:27.117 --> 00:01:29.824
Since means from a starting point until now.

28
00:01:30.417 --> 00:01:32.033
I have waited since noon.

29
00:01:32.617 --> 00:01:35.466
Your turn. Say: Since.

30
00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.197
Since.

31
00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:40.603
For.

32
00:01:41.617 --> 00:01:43.535
For means used with a length of time.

33
00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:45.697
I have waited for an hour.

34
00:01:46.283 --> 00:01:48.483
Your turn. Say: For.

35
00:01:51.333 --> 00:01:52.056
For.

36
00:01:52.817 --> 00:01:54.131
Ongoing action.

37
00:01:55.117 --> 00:01:58.150
Ongoing action means an action that has not stopped.

38
00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:00.680
Studying is an ongoing action.

39
00:02:01.283 --> 00:02:04.377
Your turn. Say: Ongoing action.

40
00:02:07.233 --> 00:02:08.490
Ongoing action.

41
00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:10.193
Recently.

42
00:02:11.183 --> 00:02:13.194
Recently means not long ago.

43
00:02:13.783 --> 00:02:15.969
I have been working a lot recently.

44
00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:18.841
Your turn. Say: Recently.

45
00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:22.771
Recently.

46
00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:27.345
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:28.183 --> 00:02:31.634
Visal, tell me about something you have been doing recently.

48
00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:43.102
I have been learning to cook. The present perfect continuous is have or has been plus the -ing form. It shows an action that started in the past and continues now.

49
00:02:44.217 --> 00:02:45.636
What do for and since do?

50
00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:58.449
For gives the duration: I have been studying for two hours. Since gives the starting point: I have been studying since eight o'clock. Both answer How long?

51
00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:01.689
How is it different from the present perfect?

52
00:03:02.783 --> 00:03:15.910
The continuous focuses on the activity and how long: I have been reading all day. The simple focuses on the result: I have read three chapters. We use the simple with state verbs.

53
00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:18.532
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:19.383 --> 00:03:25.330
Grammar focus: Present perfect continuous: have and has been plus verb-ing.

55
00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:26.817
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:27.517 --> 00:03:29.586
I have been learning to cook recently.

57
00:03:30.483 --> 00:03:32.506
She has been working since eight o'clock.

58
00:03:33.417 --> 00:03:35.312
They have been waiting for an hour.

59
00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:45.270
Use have / has been + verb-ing for actions that started in the past and continue now, or that have a present result. Use for with a period and since with a start.

60
00:03:46.017 --> 00:03:50.085
Be careful! Don't say: I am studying since two hours.

61
00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:54.788
Say: I have been studying for two hours.

62
00:03:55.088 --> 00:03:57.331
Use the present perfect continuous.

63
00:03:58.133 --> 00:04:00.867
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:02.784
Still Going.

65
00:04:03.084 --> 00:04:05.327
I have been learning to cook recently.

66
00:04:06.333 --> 00:04:08.786
My sister has been working since eight o'clock.

67
00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:11.463
They have been waiting for an hour.

68
00:04:12.467 --> 00:04:14.977
It has been raining all day, so the ground is wet.

69
00:04:15.967 --> 00:04:18.233
Duration questions begin with How long?

70
00:04:19.333 --> 00:04:23.103
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:25.566
I blank for two hours.

72
00:04:25.866 --> 00:04:29.973
A, have studied. B, have been studying. C, am study.

73
00:04:33.533 --> 00:04:36.020
The answer is B: have been studying.

74
00:04:37.183 --> 00:04:39.311
She has been working blank nine o'clock.

75
00:04:39.611 --> 00:04:42.858
A, for. B, since. C, during.

76
00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.202
The answer is B: since.

77
00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:51.106
They have been waiting blank an hour.

78
00:04:51.406 --> 00:04:54.246
A, for. B, since. C, from.

79
00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:59.521
The answer is A: for.

80
00:05:00.683 --> 00:05:02.346
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:05:02.646 --> 00:05:07.124
A, I have been know him.. B, I have known him.. C, I have been knowing him..

82
00:05:10.667 --> 00:05:12.991
The answer is B: I have known him..

83
00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:16.393
According to the reading, what is wet?

84
00:05:16.693 --> 00:05:19.929
A, the ground. B, the room. C, the table.

85
00:05:23.467 --> 00:05:25.606
The answer is A: the ground.

86
00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:30.288
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:33.858
Write a sentence about something you have been doing recently.

88
00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:44.092
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:44.392 --> 00:05:58.611
I have been practising English every evening for the last three months. I have been reading short stories and I have been writing a diary. I use the present perfect continuous because these activities continue now.

90
00:05:58.911 --> 00:06:00.725
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:01.617 --> 00:06:08.809
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and present perfect continuous: have and has been plus verb-ing.

92
00:06:09.109 --> 00:06:13.618
Today's value is diligence. Check the details carefully before you commit.

93
00:06:13.918 --> 00:06:16.408
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

94
00:06:16.708 --> 00:06:19.709
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

